From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Experimental ESP32-C3 port <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] faad2: optional 32-bit packed PS history for fixed-point SBR

Base: knik0/faad2 e8e76f0a44db45aed773a3f62fe35a63c867a738
      (FAAD2 2.11.4 release)

This is the first, deliberately conservative integration of the
ESP32-C3 packed-complex experiment.

It does NOT pack the main sbr_info::Xsbr working matrix yet.  Xsbr
requires a wider SBR/QMF slot-cache conversion and should be handled
as a separate patch.

This patch:
  * adds a 4+14+14 packed complex storage format;
  * uses a shared 4-bit exponent with shift = exponent + 3;
  * uses arithmetic truncation on store;
  * restores non-zero mantissas to the midpoint of the quantization cell;
  * preserves mantissa zero as exact zero;
  * uses branchless midpoint reconstruction;
  * uses a small compare tree instead of CLZ for exponent selection;
  * optionally replaces the four large PS delay/all-pass history arrays.

The four converted PS arrays contain 2400 complex values:

  delay_Qmf          14 * 64      =  896
  delay_SubQmf        2 * 32      =   64
  delay_Qmf_ser       3 * 5 * 64  =  960
  delay_SubQmf_ser    3 * 5 * 32  =  480
                                    ----
                                    2400 complex

With fixed-point real_t=int32_t:
  original: 2400 * 8 = 19200 bytes
  packed:   2400 * 4 =  9600 bytes
  saving:                9600 bytes (9.375 KiB)

Enable with standalone CMake:

  cmake -S . -B build \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
    -DFAAD_PACKED_PS_HISTORY=ON

and build the fixed-point target:

  cmake --build build --target faad_fixed

For ESP-IDF, add both definitions to the FAAD component:

  target_compile_definitions(${COMPONENT_LIB} PRIVATE
      FIXED_POINT
      FAAD_PACKED_PS_HISTORY
  )

The format is intentionally limited to FIXED_POINT builds.

